# SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000140  -  CAT II
# The web server must be built to fail to a known safe state if system
# initialization fails, shutdown fails, or aborts fail.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000140
group:           V-206405
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001190
control_rev5:    SC-24

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise can be configured to enter a known, safe state rather
                 than continue into failure: it pauses indexing and declines to launch
                 searches once free space on a partition falls below a configured minimum,
                 and it can be held to the file system lock check so splunkd refuses to
                 start on an unrecognized file system instead of starting and risking
                 indexed data.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] OPTIMISTIC_ABOUT_FILE_LOCKING not_equals 1, evaluated against the vendor-documented default of 0 when the setting is absent, which yields Not a Finding on this instance.
check:           server.conf [diskUsage] minFreeSpace matches ^([1-9][0-9]?(\.[0-9]+)?%|[0-9]{6,}|[1-9][0-9]{4})$
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] OPTIMISTIC_ABOUT_FILE_LOCKING not_equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] OPTIMISTIC_ABOUT_FILE_LOCKING not_equals 1, evaluated against the vendor-documented default of 0 when the setting is absent, which yields Not a Finding on this instance.
vendor:          server.conf [diskUsage] minFreeSpace https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] OPTIMISTIC_ABOUT_FILE_LOCKING https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The free-space threshold itself, which comes from the organization's risk
                 analysis - organization-defined value
external:        Service restart, crash handling and ordering behavior on initialization or
                 abort failure - operating system service manager
external:        Storage capacity monitoring and alerting on the partitions holding index
                 data - operating system and monitoring
external:        Data integrity of partially written buckets after an abort - file system

citation:        splunk-launch.conf.spec:214-220 (OPTIMISTIC_ABOUT_FILE_LOCKING = [0|1];
                 "CAUTION: USE THIS SETTING AT YOUR OWN RISK. YOU CAN LOSE ANY DATA THAT
                 HAS BEEN INDEXED WHILE THE SETTING IS ACTIVE"; when set to 1 Splunk
                 software skips the file system check and splunkd starts whether or not it
                 can recognize the file system); server.conf.spec:1858-1881 (minFreeSpace =
                 <num>|<percentage>, "Specifies a safe amount of space that must exist for
                 splunkd to continue operating"; indexing is paused and a warning posted;
                 default 5000); server.conf.spec:1883-1890 (pollingFrequency default
                 100000, pollingTimerFrequency default 10)
finding:         The application is not configured to fail to a known state to the extent
                 the product allows: the file system lock check is being skipped
                 (OPTIMISTIC_ABOUT_FILE_LOCKING is 1), or the minimum free space at which
                 splunkd stops operating is not expressed in configuration.
